# KourOS backend — environment. Copy to .env (compose reads it via env_file).
# All optional in dev: with no key set, weaveAuth falls back to a dev identity stub.

# Identity (jkAuth). In prod set ONE of these to verify the jkos_token signature:
#   JKOS_AUTH_JWKS_URI   preferred — JWKS-by-kid, supports key rotation
#   JKOS_AUTH_PUBLIC_KEY the static RSA public key (PEM)
# JKOS_AUTH_JWKS_URI=https://auth.jkos.net/auth/.well-known/jwks.json
# JKOS_AUTH_PUBLIC_KEY=
# JKOS_AUTH_ISSUER=jkos-auth         # staging uses jkos-auth-staging

# Cross-origin: the shell origin + any extra peers allowed to call this API.
# SHELL_URL=https://jkos.net
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://beigeboard.jkos.net

# Runtime (compose sets these; defaults are fine for local `npm start`).
# PORT=3011
# DB_PATH=/data/kouros.db
# STATIC_DIR=/app/dist

# Library scanner: folder the boot scan + rescanLibrary walk, recursively — every
# audio file found anywhere under it becomes one `tracks` row (mp3/m4a/aac/flac/
# ogg/opus/wav). Cover art is extracted alongside the database (<DB_PATH dir>/
# covers/<id>.jpg).
#
# Both compose files now bind the real library read-only at /music and set
# MUSIC_DIR to match, so this only needs setting for a bare `npm start`.
# MUSIC_DIR=/music
# MUSIC_PATH=/mnt/Luna/Luna/Plex/Music  # compose: the HOST path bound to /music
#
# ⚠️ On the TrueNAS host the Luna share is the dataset at /mnt/Luna/Luna — a
# workstation mounts the same share at /mnt/Luna, so the library is
# /mnt/Luna/Luna/Plex/Music there and /mnt/Luna/Plex/Music is a DIFFERENT, empty
# directory. Docker auto-creates a missing bind source instead of failing, so the
# wrong path mounts cleanly and the scan finds zero files with no error anywhere.

# Folder NAMES the scan refuses to enter, at any depth under MUSIC_DIR.
# Comma-separated. Unset uses the default below; set to the EMPTY string to scan
# everything. `Old (Needs to be trimmed)` is the previous artist-nested rip, still
# sitting inside the library root — ~15,000 files that duplicate the flat
# re-download beside them. Keep this in step with `music/config.py`'s
# EXCLUDE_DIRS: they are separate lists (the embedder has zero jkOS imports by
# design), and drift shows up as tracks that list fine but have no vectors.
# MUSIC_EXCLUDE_DIRS=Old (Needs to be trimmed)

# ── The music embedder's index (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Source of the CLAP vectors behind /api/discover/* — similarity, radio, Runs and
# the vibe map. Produced by the separate Python pipeline in music/ (ToDo §8) and
# read STRICTLY READ-ONLY here; KourOS never computes an embedding.
#
# Entirely optional. With no index — or for any track the backfill has not reached
# yet — every discovery surface falls back to metadata affinity (artist/genre/era)
# and REPORTS that it did, so the app is quieter rather than broken.
#
# music/index.db is gitignored, so it does not arrive with a deploy: copy it onto
# the data volume. ⚠️ Copy the `-wal` sidecar with it — the embedder runs in WAL
# mode, and taking the .db alone gives you whatever snapshot predated the last
# checkpoint, i.e. silently fewer vectors than were actually computed.
#
#   scp music/index.db music/index.db-wal truenas:/mnt/Luna/Backends/Staging/kouros-data/
#   # (renaming index.db -> music-index.db, the default below)
#
# VECTOR_DB_PATH=/data/music-index.db

# The directory name the embedder's stored paths are rooted at. Used to recover an
# artist/title key when the index was built against a DIFFERENT library layout than
# the one being scanned — see backend/src/discover/vectors.js's header for why a
# plain path join is not enough. Defaults to the basename of MUSIC_DIR.
# LIBRARY_ROOT_NAME=Music
